From: =?UTF-8?q?Bj=C3=B8rn=20Inge=20Berg?= <b.inge@nightscoutfoundation.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:31:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Pair with libre2sim in the iOS Simulator

The Simulator has no NFC. On Simulator builds only, Libre 2 pairing asks
libre2sim's HTTP API (LIBRE2SIM_URL, default http://127.0.0.1:8081) the
questions SensorPairingService asks over CoreNFC, in the same order, and
puts the answers through the same checks.

SimulatedSensorPairingService lives in its own file, compiled only for the
Simulator. It gets the enable-streaming command from SensorPairingService's
own nfcCommand (now fileprivate) through a Simulator-only extension, so the
two cannot drift apart. Device builds compile to the same code as before.
---
 Features.swift                                |   4 +
 .../SensorPairing/SensorPairingService.swift  |  13 +-
 .../SimulatedSensorPairingService.swift       | 158 ++++++++++++++++++
 LibreTransmitter.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj    |   4 +
 .../LibreTransmitterManagerV3.swift           |   4 +
 5 files changed, 182 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 LibreSensor/SensorPairing/SimulatedSensorPairingService.swift

